This covers the metrics, extracted triples, knowledge graphs, generated
reports, confusion matrices, threshold sweeps, ablation outputs and figures
produced by the pipeline.


Material NOT covered by the licence above
-----------------------------------------

DERIVED DATASET COLUMNS. The files

    results/cicids/<model>/community_assignments.csv

carry, alongside the pipeline's own outputs, sixteen feature columns
reproduced from the CIC-IDS-2017 dataset, including Flow Duration, Total Fwd
Packets, SYN Flag Count, Flow Bytes/s, Average Packet Size and the class
Label. Those columns are not original to this work and are not relicensed
here. They remain subject to the terms set by the Canadian Institute for
Cybersecurity, University of New Brunswick, which permit research use and
require that the dataset be cited:

    I. Sharafaldin, A. Habibi Lashkari and A. A. Ghorbani, "Toward Generating
    a New Intrusion Detection Dataset and Intrusion Traffic Characterization,"
    in Proceedings of the 4th International Conference on Information Systems
    Security and Privacy (ICISSP), 2018.

    https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/ids-2017.html

The columns are included because they are what makes the clustering and the
per-community scoring reproducible. If you redistribute these files, carry the
CIC citation requirement with them.

DARPA TRANSPARENT COMPUTING. Outputs under results/darpa/ are derived from the
CADETS E3 engagement data and the accompanying ground-truth report, released
by the DARPA Transparent Computing program. Ground-truth technique sets were
transcribed by hand from that report.

    https://github.com/darpa-i2o/Transparent-Computing

MITRE ATT&CK. Technique identifiers, names and procedure descriptions are from
the MITRE ATT&CK knowledge base, (c) The MITRE Corporation, and are used under
MITRE's terms of use. ATT&CK is a registered trademark of The MITRE
Corporation.

    https://attack.mitre.org/resources/terms-of-use/
